          "Histamine on **endothelial H1 receptors** opens post-capillary venule junctions, so plasma leaks into the **superficial dermis (wheal)**; on **sensory C fibres** it causes itch; and an **axon reflex** releasing substance P and CGRP gives the surrounding **flare** - the triple response of Lewis. [Rook 10e 2024]",
